    "info1": "The soccer park combines football and golf with lots of fun. Here, those who play tactically and keep a cool head have a chance.",
    "info2": "This fun sport comes from Scandinavia. About 15 years ago football golf was played there for the first time. Now this sport is very popular - there are about 30 football golf courses there.",
    "info3": "In the spring of 2006, the first site was opened in Germany. Since then, the sport has spread throughout Germany. There are currently about 20 sites, and new ones are added every year.",
    "info4": "Various championships are now held on these sites every year. There is also a world association (\"World Footballgolf Association\"), which hosts a world championship and a European championship every year.",
    "info5": "Our site in Salzburg is the first in Austria.",
    "info6": "Football golf is played like golf on 18 holes with par 72. A ball is played with the foot without using a club with as few \"strokes\" as possible over various obstacles to the hole.",
    "info7": "Our open-air football golf course covers a playing area of ​​around 32,000 square meters. The lanes are between 50 and 175 meters long, the total distance of all 18 lanes together is about 2 km.",
    "info8": "It takes around 1.5 - 2 hours to enjoy this extraordinary fun to the fullest!",
    "info9": "This new fun sport is ideal for families, companies, clubs, birthdays, groups or simply with friends.",
    "info10": "Experienced soccer players do not always have an advantage! Professional teams have also been regular customers at the existing sites in Scandinavia and Germany for years.",
    "info11": "Football golf is ideal for team building events!",

    "orderA1": "Use of the soccerpark is at your own risk.",
    "orderA2": "Drunk guests are not allowed in.",
    "orderA3": "Please do not enter the lanes after the round has been played.",
    "orderA4": "Children only when accompanied and supervised by an adult.",
    "order1": "Please do not bring your own food or drinks to the facility.",
    "order2": "Please do not wear soccer shoes with cleats.",
    "order3": "Please adhere to the maximum group size of 5 players per flight.",
    "order4": "Please allow smaller groups to overtake.",
    "order5": "Please put the rubbish in the appropriate bins.",
    "order6": "Please do not take any dogs on the course.",
    "order7": "In the event of a storm or lightning strike, please leave the facility immediately and do not seek shelter on the course.",
    "order8": "Please enter and leave the facility only via the main entrance.",
    "order9": "Please do not bring your own sound system.",
    "order10": "Please be considerate of families and children.",
    "order11": "Parents are responsible for their children and have a duty of supervision.",
    
    "rules_title": "Welcome to Soccerpark Salzburg!",
    "rules1": "In order to have a fair comparison, soccergolf has very clear guidelines and rules of the game. Of course, in the end, the person who needed the fewest shots always won.    ",
    "rules2": "Each fairway has its own description: a track board. Here you can clearly see the layout of the fairway and the kick-off point on the green mat. So before you play a fairway, please always look at this lane board carefully.",
    "rules3": "The red arrows next to the obstacles indicate in which direction the ball has to go through the obstacle. If the ball is accidentally shot past the obstacle, it must be played back in order to then be able to go through the obstacle in the right direction.",
    "rules4": "The kick-off always happens from the green mat. The ball must be placed on or behind the white line. The goal is always a flag with a certain type of hole.",
    "rules5": "If the ball is in the rough (to the right or left of the fairway) or in a bunker, it must be played from there. However, if the ball is shot down a side lane, it is out of bounds and must be replaced to the last starting position from which it was played and one penalty point must be added.",
    "rules6": "It is important that the players in a group always play together: everyone in the group shoots their ball once and remembers its position. The one whose ball is farthest from the target takes the second shot first. Then everyone else in the group continues in the same order. And so it goes on until the balls are sunk in the hole. When the ball is in the hole, the number of shots required is noted on the scorecard or in the app.",
    "rules7": "If a ball is in the way, it can either be played or secured with a marker. However, if a ball is accidentally kicked, the kicked ball is replaced and the other ball is left where it rolls out.",
    "rules8": "The maximum number of shots is calculated from the par specification. This is visible on every track board, on the scorecard and in this app. The maximum number of shots is always twice the par value. For example, on a par 3 fairway, the ball must go in the target hole by the 6th shot at the latest. If this is not the case, a penalty point must be added, i.e., you have to note down 7 shots. There are par 3, par 4, par 5 and par 6 holes on the course.",
    "rules9": "There is a water obstacle on lane 9. For safety reasons, entering the water is strictly prohibited. Balls that land in the water can be retrieved with the landing net. You can find the special regulation on the track board.",
    "rules10": "Our toilets are located at the end of the building and are signposted. We attach great importance to order and cleanliness and we ask you to dispose rubbish in the appropriate containers.",
    "rules11": "Of course, we ask that celebrating groups be considerate of other guests throughout the facility, especially families and children. Please do not use any sound systems on the facility!",
    "rules12": "For reasons of fair play and to avoid major traffic jams, larger groups will allow smaller groups to overtake. The ideal and maximum group size is 4-5 people!",
    "rules13": "A special note for children's birthday parties: Parents are responsible for supervising their children!",
    "rules14": "When a track is finished, please leave it quickly! After completing the 18 holes, please always return the balls in groups to the cash desk! You are of course welcome to buy a 2nd round or a day ticket from us at a reduced price.",
    "rules15": "We are happy to provide you with cool drinks, ice cream and snacks. Please do not bring your own food or drinks to the facility!",
    "rules16": "As a special service we offer you free WLAN. If you liked it with us, we would be very happy to receive positive feedback!",
    "rules17": "You can get gift vouchers for every occasion at the checkout. If you have any questions or requests, just come to us - we will be happy to help you!",

    "rules_wagrain_title": "Welcome to Soccerpark Wagrain-Kleinarl!",
    "rules_wagrain_8": "The maximum number of shots is calculated from the par specification. This is visible on every track board, on the scorecard and in this app. The maximum number of shots is always twice the par value. For example, on a par 3 fairway, the ball must go in the target hole by the 6th shot at the latest. If this is not the case, a penalty point must be added, i.e., you have to note down 7 shots. There are par 3, par 4 and par 5 holes on the course.",
    "rules_wagrain_10": "Our toilets are located in the ticket office building and are signposted. We attach great importance to order and cleanliness and we ask you to dispose rubbish in the appropriate containers.",
    
